  "verbalization": "Usararotenoid C appears to be a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Dendocarbin K and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, all of which ultimately target KB. This suggests a chain of interactions where Usararotenoid C may influence KB through the intermediate of SNU-387. The evidence points to a potential mechanism where Usararotenoid C modulates the activity of SNU-387, which then affects KB via a series of downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Usararotenoid C in regulating KB through a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving receptor binding or enzyme inhibition. The evidence supports a dependency on SNU-387 as a critical mediator in the relationship between Usararotenoid C and KB, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the exact molecular mechanism.",
